1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,253
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

2
00:00:03,336 --> 00:00:08,341
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

3
00:00:08,425 --> 00:00:10,593
- <i>♪ Fix it</i> ♪
- <i>♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

4
00:00:10,677 --> 00:00:12,679
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

5
00:00:12,762 --> 00:00:15,807
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

6
00:00:16,725 --> 00:00:18,643
This doesn't come off easily.

7
00:00:18,727 --> 00:00:20,937
[grunting]

8
00:00:21,771 --> 00:00:23,148
Could it be I left it there?

9
00:00:23,231 --> 00:00:24,315
Is this what you're looking for?

10
00:00:25,358 --> 00:00:27,318
[screaming]

11
00:00:27,402 --> 00:00:28,778
[gasping]

12
00:00:28,862 --> 00:00:30,864
Maybe you should go to the wake tomorrow.

13
00:00:30,947 --> 00:00:32,574
[Atoy] I suspect

14
00:00:32,657 --> 00:00:34,701
what happened to Tonet wasn't an accident.

15
00:00:34,784 --> 00:00:35,702
What do you mean?

16
00:00:35,785 --> 00:00:37,746
Because I went back to the place
where she died.

17
00:00:37,829 --> 00:00:41,416
[Atoy] <i>I found a piece of evidence</i>
<i>that might have been left behind.</i>

18
00:00:41,499 --> 00:00:42,667
[indistinct chattering]

19
00:00:42,751 --> 00:00:44,627
[in English] This is
my sister-in-law, Martina,

20
00:00:44,711 --> 00:00:45,712
and her son, Gavin.

21
00:00:45,795 --> 00:00:47,338
[in English] My condolences.

22
00:00:47,422 --> 00:00:49,632
[Atoy] Ah, sorry, I just
got distracted by your bag.

23
00:00:49,716 --> 00:00:53,219
But it seems to be missing
one stud, like… this?

24
00:00:53,303 --> 00:00:55,013
[in English] Um,
I'm just gonna get a drink.

25
00:00:55,096 --> 00:00:56,306
[in English] Excuse me.

26
00:00:57,348 --> 00:00:59,100
Where were you all day yesterday?

27
00:00:59,184 --> 00:01:00,310
Were you at a mall?

28
00:01:00,393 --> 00:01:03,188
The same mall where Tonet
had the accident?

29
00:01:03,271 --> 00:01:04,981
- You killed my sister?!
- [in English] Let me go!

30
00:01:05,065 --> 00:01:06,441
[Emerson] You killed my sister?!

31
00:01:06,524 --> 00:01:07,859
- [Martina, in English] Let me go!
- [Emerson] Huh!? Do it!

32
00:01:07,942 --> 00:01:08,818
How dare you!

33
00:01:08,902 --> 00:01:10,278
Did you come here just to make sure

34
00:01:10,361 --> 00:01:11,905
that my sister was killed?!

35
00:01:11,988 --> 00:01:13,573
I came here
to respectfully offer condolences!

36
00:01:13,656 --> 00:01:14,783
[in English] And then, you're gonna
accuse me of such things?!

37
00:01:14,866 --> 00:01:16,868
- [in English] Enough!
- You're not family!

38
00:01:16,951 --> 00:01:19,287
[in English] She's accusing me of killing
some girl that I don't even know!

39
00:01:19,370 --> 00:01:22,082
Because killing isn't new to this family!

40
00:01:22,165 --> 00:01:23,875
It's like we never did anything right!

41
00:01:23,958 --> 00:01:25,418
[Red] <i>Let it go.</i>

42
00:01:26,085 --> 00:01:28,588
What's important
is we know what Atoy is thinking.

43
00:01:29,255 --> 00:01:30,381
[in English] So, what are you gonna do?

44
00:01:30,465 --> 00:01:33,593
That evidence… We need to divert it.

45
00:01:33,676 --> 00:01:36,095
PREVIOUSLY

46
00:01:37,055 --> 00:01:38,306
[music fades]

47
00:01:51,736 --> 00:01:52,987
Bro…

48
00:01:54,781 --> 00:01:56,157
Are you okay?

49
00:02:00,203 --> 00:02:02,622
[muffled chattering in the distance]

50
00:02:02,705 --> 00:02:04,582
I saw it in her eyes.

51
00:02:05,291 --> 00:02:06,835
She really looked guilty.

52
00:02:07,669 --> 00:02:09,295
[pensive music playing]

53
00:02:09,379 --> 00:02:10,713
Even so,

54
00:02:10,797 --> 00:02:12,507
you still shouldn't have strangled her.

55
00:02:13,299 --> 00:02:15,343
She could sue you for that.

56
00:02:19,639 --> 00:02:22,225
I'm serious. I'll really
file a case against her.

57
00:02:23,351 --> 00:02:25,687
Based on your evidence.

58
00:02:29,691 --> 00:02:30,859
Bro…

59
00:02:33,361 --> 00:02:36,447
That's a bit unclear.
It's still not enough evidence.

60
00:02:37,657 --> 00:02:39,409
What I find even more puzzling,

61
00:02:40,326 --> 00:02:43,538
is that if it's true, what's her motive?

62
00:02:47,500 --> 00:02:50,169
We'll find out once she's investigated.

63
00:02:50,879 --> 00:02:54,883
I'll get help from my lawyer client.

64
00:02:58,553 --> 00:02:59,596
[Emerson] 'Toy…

65
00:03:00,346 --> 00:03:03,308
If things get messy,

66
00:03:03,391 --> 00:03:04,934
whose side are you on?

67
00:03:05,018 --> 00:03:07,562
[suspicious music playing]

68
00:03:07,645 --> 00:03:11,107
The mother of your child
is from that Regalia family.

69
00:03:12,400 --> 00:03:14,235
Theirs or mine?

70
00:03:15,069 --> 00:03:19,365
I don't want us to clash again.

71
00:03:30,126 --> 00:03:32,086
As long as we're on the right side.

72
00:03:34,464 --> 00:03:35,965
[music fades]

73
00:03:36,925 --> 00:03:39,135
Just don't leave me hanging, okay?

74
00:03:39,219 --> 00:03:43,306
[tense music playing]

75
00:03:53,274 --> 00:03:54,817
[music fades]

76
00:03:54,901 --> 00:03:59,530
[suave theme music playing]

77
00:03:59,614 --> 00:04:01,449
[motorcycle revving]

78
00:04:11,251 --> 00:04:13,836
[gunshots]

79
00:04:13,920 --> 00:04:14,921
[clicking]

80
00:04:15,004 --> 00:04:17,465
[snipping]

81
00:04:17,548 --> 00:04:18,925
[music swells]

82
00:04:19,008 --> 00:04:23,179
[electronic blipping]

83
00:04:26,224 --> 00:04:28,226
[Dmitri] Do you fairly believe that

84
00:04:29,060 --> 00:04:31,771
Martina is guilty of that girl's death,

85
00:04:32,313 --> 00:04:36,484
based only on Atoy's
informal investigation?

86
00:04:36,567 --> 00:04:39,570
Dad, you know Atoy.

87
00:04:39,654 --> 00:04:40,863
He's a tracker.

88
00:04:41,489 --> 00:04:43,408
[in English] He knows what he's doing.

89
00:04:44,951 --> 00:04:46,160
[in English] That's true.

90
00:04:47,412 --> 00:04:51,833
But we both know
that Atoy is biased against Red

91
00:04:52,709 --> 00:04:54,544
because they fought before.

92
00:04:56,004 --> 00:04:59,716
What if he just made a mistake?

93
00:05:00,466 --> 00:05:03,886
What if he's just looking
for someone to blame

94
00:05:03,970 --> 00:05:06,681
to appease the family of the deceased?

95
00:05:07,640 --> 00:05:08,725
[in English] Look.

96
00:05:09,726 --> 00:05:11,394
[in English] They're not perfect.

97
00:05:12,437 --> 00:05:15,815
[in English] But you're too hard
on Red and Martina.

98
00:05:16,441 --> 00:05:20,236
Martina did everything
she could to find your child.

99
00:05:21,946 --> 00:05:25,366
She already apologized
to you for all her mistakes.

100
00:05:25,867 --> 00:05:30,038
Now, if she's guilty,
I won't side with her.

101
00:05:30,997 --> 00:05:34,667
[in English] But you have to give her
the benefit of the doubt.

102
00:05:35,209 --> 00:05:39,047
After all, she's still your family.

103
00:05:39,130 --> 00:05:43,259
So, please, believe her innocence first.

104
00:05:44,260 --> 00:05:47,096
[pensive music playing]

105
00:05:54,145 --> 00:05:55,313
[clears throat]

106
00:05:55,938 --> 00:05:57,023
[in English] Hi, Ms. Audrey!

107
00:05:57,106 --> 00:05:59,192
Ria here, secretary of Ma'am Martina.

108
00:05:59,275 --> 00:06:00,860
We have a breakfast meeting.

109
00:06:01,444 --> 00:06:02,361
[in English] Ah, okay.

110
00:06:02,445 --> 00:06:05,198
Uh, Martina will be out in a while.

111
00:06:08,201 --> 00:06:09,535
[suspicious music playing]

112
00:06:09,619 --> 00:06:12,330
It's just the two of us here.
Be honest with me.

113
00:06:12,413 --> 00:06:13,790
Where were you really yesterday?

114
00:06:13,873 --> 00:06:15,666
[in English] I was at my office!

115
00:06:15,750 --> 00:06:17,251
At Bahay Kayakap!

116
00:06:20,296 --> 00:06:22,090
Ria, right?

117
00:06:22,173 --> 00:06:23,382
Yes.

118
00:06:23,466 --> 00:06:28,096
Um, was Martina
at the office the other day?

119
00:06:28,179 --> 00:06:30,890
[in English] Around 12 p.m. onwards?

120
00:06:30,973 --> 00:06:32,058
Yes, ma'am.

121
00:06:32,141 --> 00:06:33,434
[dramatic sting]

122
00:06:33,518 --> 00:06:34,727
Uh, are you sure?

123
00:06:34,811 --> 00:06:36,729
As in you saw her?

124
00:06:36,813 --> 00:06:37,980
Yes, ma'am.

125
00:06:38,064 --> 00:06:40,525
Actually, she even asked me to buy lunch.

126
00:06:40,608 --> 00:06:42,193
I have a picture…

127
00:06:42,276 --> 00:06:43,986
You can see her in the background.

128
00:06:45,321 --> 00:06:46,405
Here.

129
00:06:50,743 --> 00:06:52,787
- Is there more?
- Yes, ma'am.

130
00:06:53,579 --> 00:06:58,459
- [dramatic sting]
- [tense music playing]

131
00:07:02,380 --> 00:07:04,674
Ah, ma'am, I'll just prepare
my presentation.

132
00:07:04,757 --> 00:07:06,050
Oh-- Okay, okay.

133
00:07:06,134 --> 00:07:07,051
Thank you.

134
00:07:10,388 --> 00:07:11,431
[helper] Ma'am?

135
00:07:11,514 --> 00:07:13,015
Ma'am, excuse me.

136
00:07:13,099 --> 00:07:16,144
I saw this under the console table
when I was cleaning.

137
00:07:16,227 --> 00:07:18,354
I don't know what it's for.

138
00:07:19,856 --> 00:07:21,190
Ah-- Okay, okay.

139
00:07:21,274 --> 00:07:22,692
[helper] Okay, ma'am.

140
00:07:22,775 --> 00:07:24,777
[tense sinister music playing]

141
00:07:25,653 --> 00:07:26,571
What's that?

142
00:07:29,991 --> 00:07:31,659
[in English] Bag stud.

143
00:07:32,827 --> 00:07:36,998
Like the one from Martina's bag.

144
00:07:38,624 --> 00:07:39,834
Let me see.

145
00:07:42,545 --> 00:07:44,839
Is this the bag stud she lost?

146
00:07:46,507 --> 00:07:50,344
Does this look like
the one Atoy saw at the mall?

147
00:07:58,019 --> 00:08:02,106
Ah, sir, maybe I should be the one
to give it to Ma'am Martina.

148
00:08:02,190 --> 00:08:03,566
[music fades]

149
00:08:06,235 --> 00:08:10,698
[in English] I think Martina deserves
an apology from you.

150
00:08:10,781 --> 00:08:13,493
[dramatic sting]

151
00:08:26,214 --> 00:08:28,758
[siren blaring]

152
00:08:29,717 --> 00:08:36,474
[muffled chattering in the distance]

153
00:08:40,061 --> 00:08:41,020
[pensive music playing]

154
00:08:41,103 --> 00:08:42,688
How's Emerson?

155
00:08:43,439 --> 00:08:44,398
[Atoy] Mmm.

156
00:08:45,650 --> 00:08:47,401
You, how are you?

157
00:08:47,485 --> 00:08:49,362
Have you spoken to Martina?

158
00:08:50,488 --> 00:08:53,449
So, Emerson is really
going to file a case.

159
00:08:54,283 --> 00:08:57,703
You know, at first,
I really thought Martina was involved.

160
00:08:58,287 --> 00:09:01,457
That's why I didn't defend her
when you all ganged up on her.

161
00:09:02,458 --> 00:09:04,835
[in English] But now,
I really think I was wrong.

162
00:09:04,919 --> 00:09:08,422
[somber music playing]

163
00:09:09,757 --> 00:09:11,467
- How can you say that?
- Because…

164
00:09:12,301 --> 00:09:14,345
When Tonet had the accident,

165
00:09:14,428 --> 00:09:16,764
Martina was in the office
with her secretary.

166
00:09:16,847 --> 00:09:18,766
I saw some pictures.

167
00:09:19,684 --> 00:09:21,727
And that stud you found…

168
00:09:22,395 --> 00:09:24,105
[in English] I don't think it was hers.

169
00:09:24,689 --> 00:09:27,608
Because our maid found a stud at home.

170
00:09:28,901 --> 00:09:33,573
I feel like Martina's bag stud
came off at home, not at the mall.

171
00:09:33,656 --> 00:09:35,908
[suspicious music playing]

172
00:09:35,992 --> 00:09:38,369
And I feel so bad because…

173
00:09:38,452 --> 00:09:40,079
I confronted Martina.

174
00:09:41,080 --> 00:09:43,541
I insinuated that

175
00:09:43,624 --> 00:09:45,418
she was a killer.

176
00:09:46,961 --> 00:09:49,171
[in English] But now,
it looks like she's innocent.

177
00:09:55,886 --> 00:09:57,305
[music fades]

178
00:09:57,388 --> 00:09:59,932
Are you sure she believed
I was at the office?

179
00:10:00,016 --> 00:10:01,058
Of course, ma'am.

180
00:10:01,142 --> 00:10:02,768
I even showed the selfie,

181
00:10:02,852 --> 00:10:05,313
with you busy at work in the background.

182
00:10:05,396 --> 00:10:07,273
[in English] That's the magic of AI.

183
00:10:08,274 --> 00:10:10,234
- [in English] See?
- [in English] Very good, Ria.

184
00:10:10,318 --> 00:10:11,235
[dramatic sting]

185
00:10:11,319 --> 00:10:14,030
Ma'am, don't forget
my salary increase, okay? You promised.

186
00:10:14,113 --> 00:10:15,114
Of course!

187
00:10:15,197 --> 00:10:17,033
As long as you're loyal to me.

188
00:10:17,116 --> 00:10:18,659
By the way, ma'am…

189
00:10:19,660 --> 00:10:22,413
Was that bag stud we found yours?

190
00:10:25,791 --> 00:10:27,543
- Has Audrey seen this?
- [Ria] Yes.

191
00:10:27,627 --> 00:10:29,503
She even stared at it closely.

192
00:10:29,587 --> 00:10:32,965
[suspicious music playing]

193
00:10:46,437 --> 00:10:47,647
Nanny.

194
00:10:47,730 --> 00:10:48,856
[helper] Ma'am?

195
00:10:51,859 --> 00:10:56,405
Do you remember my favorite bag
with those metal designs?

196
00:10:56,489 --> 00:10:58,407
One of them came off.

197
00:10:58,491 --> 00:10:59,659
If you see it, please tell me,

198
00:10:59,742 --> 00:11:02,119
or you can give it to Audrey
if you can't find me.

199
00:11:02,203 --> 00:11:03,496
Yes, ma'am.

200
00:11:03,579 --> 00:11:04,997
[in English] Thank you.

201
00:11:05,081 --> 00:11:07,583
[music swells]

202
00:11:12,797 --> 00:11:14,799
[in English] I'm such a freaking genius.

203
00:11:15,383 --> 00:11:17,593
Audrey will swallow
everything she said to me.

204
00:11:17,676 --> 00:11:18,803
[in English] Oh my gosh.

205
00:11:23,391 --> 00:11:25,142
[music fades]

206
00:11:25,226 --> 00:11:27,978
This is what you saw
at the scene of the accident, right?

207
00:11:28,062 --> 00:11:29,647
[in English] Yes, Attorney.

208
00:11:29,730 --> 00:11:33,609
Oh, that matches what
we saw Martina carrying,

209
00:11:33,692 --> 00:11:35,653
so she can't deny it.

210
00:11:35,736 --> 00:11:37,905
[in English] Okay. Highly suggestive,

211
00:11:37,988 --> 00:11:42,535
but it does not rise to the level
of establishing criminal liability.

212
00:11:42,618 --> 00:11:44,036
- [in English] Okay.
- [in English] Suspicion alone

213
00:11:44,120 --> 00:11:45,371
is insufficient.

214
00:11:45,454 --> 00:11:51,043
Without clear and convincing
proof of intent and unlawful conduct,

215
00:11:51,127 --> 00:11:53,671
no crime can be legally imputed.

216
00:11:53,754 --> 00:11:56,048
[pensive music playing]

217
00:11:56,132 --> 00:11:57,049
What?

218
00:11:57,133 --> 00:12:00,970
Emerson, you can file
a case against Martina Regalia,

219
00:12:01,053 --> 00:12:03,764
but it's very unlikely you'll win.

220
00:12:03,848 --> 00:12:06,058
Unless there's an eyewitness

221
00:12:06,142 --> 00:12:08,769
or you can prove
that the perfume Atoy smelled

222
00:12:08,853 --> 00:12:12,940
and this bag stud
are exclusively Martina's.

223
00:12:13,023 --> 00:12:14,859
Because, look.

224
00:12:20,698 --> 00:12:24,452
There are many bags
that have studs like this.

225
00:12:27,746 --> 00:12:29,707
What should I do?

226
00:12:29,790 --> 00:12:31,792
Emerson, I don't want you to suffer,

227
00:12:31,876 --> 00:12:33,794
and if you ask me,

228
00:12:33,878 --> 00:12:35,337
I would advise against it.

229
00:12:35,421 --> 00:12:36,255
[dramatic sting]

230
00:12:36,338 --> 00:12:41,010
[in English] Filing without solid grounds
risks an immediate dismissal.

231
00:12:41,093 --> 00:12:43,179
You could even face unnecessary costs

232
00:12:43,262 --> 00:12:45,139
and even counterclaims.

233
00:12:45,222 --> 00:12:47,975
Looks like Attorney is right, 'Son.

234
00:12:49,643 --> 00:12:52,688
Looks like we were wrong
to accuse Martina.

235
00:12:53,939 --> 00:12:55,316
So that's it?

236
00:12:55,399 --> 00:12:56,650
[sniffs]

237
00:12:57,234 --> 00:12:59,111
[Emerson] So that's it, 'Toy?

238
00:13:00,362 --> 00:13:01,697
[scoffs]

239
00:13:04,074 --> 00:13:06,327
I wish you hadn't told me.

240
00:13:07,828 --> 00:13:11,207
I wish you hadn't told me your suspicions.

241
00:13:12,041 --> 00:13:13,918
So, I wouldn't have hoped for nothing.

242
00:13:15,586 --> 00:13:18,923
[epic music playing]

243
00:13:20,466 --> 00:13:21,884
'Son.

244
00:13:29,350 --> 00:13:30,518
[in English] Boss.

245
00:13:31,644 --> 00:13:33,729
Boss Red already gave an order.

246
00:13:33,812 --> 00:13:37,233
Find out if Emerson
will file a case against his wife.

247
00:13:37,733 --> 00:13:42,029
Boss, if Emerson pushes through
with his complaint,

248
00:13:42,821 --> 00:13:44,532
what will happen to him?

249
00:13:44,615 --> 00:13:46,575
He'll just lose.

250
00:13:47,618 --> 00:13:50,412
But Boss Red is brutal when he's angry.

251
00:13:50,496 --> 00:13:53,290
Emerson might end up like his sister.

252
00:13:53,374 --> 00:13:54,250
[tense music playing]

253
00:13:54,333 --> 00:13:55,834
He's bound to lose anyway.

254
00:13:56,752 --> 00:13:58,963
So, why does something
have to happen to him?

255
00:13:59,046 --> 00:14:00,839
Why do you have so many opinions?

256
00:14:00,923 --> 00:14:02,258
Did anyone ask you?

257
00:14:02,341 --> 00:14:04,093
Just follow orders!

258
00:14:05,469 --> 00:14:06,595
Sorry.

259
00:14:15,271 --> 00:14:16,855
[music fades]

260
00:14:21,777 --> 00:14:23,779
[Emerson] How am I supposed
to eat all of this?

261
00:14:23,863 --> 00:14:25,781
[somber music playing]

262
00:14:25,865 --> 00:14:27,616
This is your fault too.

263
00:14:29,076 --> 00:14:29,910
It's your fault,

264
00:14:29,994 --> 00:14:35,124
because if I hadn't planned
to eat lechon that day,

265
00:14:36,792 --> 00:14:38,919
maybe Tonet wouldn't
have been at the mall.

266
00:14:40,296 --> 00:14:43,424
Maybe she'd still be here with me now.

267
00:14:44,717 --> 00:14:45,885
[sighs]

268
00:14:45,968 --> 00:14:48,095
[gentle music playing]

269
00:14:48,178 --> 00:14:49,179
[Atoy] 'Son?

270
00:14:53,058 --> 00:14:55,352
There's no Emerson here.

271
00:15:00,608 --> 00:15:02,276
Ah, looks like there really isn't.

272
00:15:04,194 --> 00:15:08,490
Looks like my cheerful friend is gone.

273
00:15:09,992 --> 00:15:11,994
My handsome friend,

274
00:15:12,077 --> 00:15:13,787
who's not too grumpy.

275
00:15:16,957 --> 00:15:18,208
Oh.

276
00:15:19,293 --> 00:15:21,295
This is the receipt from the coffee shop.

277
00:15:21,378 --> 00:15:23,297
[pensive music playing]

278
00:15:23,380 --> 00:15:25,633
[Atoy grunts] I paid for it

279
00:15:25,716 --> 00:15:27,343
because you walked out.

280
00:15:27,885 --> 00:15:29,345
Hey, pay me back, okay.

281
00:15:35,726 --> 00:15:37,269
This is so expensive.

282
00:15:38,270 --> 00:15:39,647
[Atoy] Oh?

283
00:15:42,483 --> 00:15:44,485
That's not expensive at all.

284
00:15:44,568 --> 00:15:46,111
What would you rather pay for? That?

285
00:15:46,195 --> 00:15:49,156
It's more expensive
if you cover the attorney's fees.

286
00:15:49,239 --> 00:15:50,658
That's a lot too.

287
00:15:50,741 --> 00:15:53,827
It looks like you don't stand
a chance in that case, bro.

288
00:16:04,880 --> 00:16:07,466
I thought we were going
to fight this, bro?

289
00:16:09,802 --> 00:16:14,932
[suspicious music playing]

290
00:16:16,767 --> 00:16:18,310
Bro…

291
00:16:24,191 --> 00:16:25,359
Nothing.

292
00:16:26,276 --> 00:16:31,949
Our evidence against Martina is weak.
The evidence is her bag and her perfume.

293
00:16:35,577 --> 00:16:37,413
I spoke with Audrey.

294
00:16:38,789 --> 00:16:39,790
[music fades]

295
00:16:39,873 --> 00:16:41,250
She said…

296
00:16:43,711 --> 00:16:47,089
Martina was really
at the office when it happened.

297
00:16:47,172 --> 00:16:48,882
They have evidence.

298
00:16:48,966 --> 00:16:50,759
She wasn't at the mall.

299
00:16:51,260 --> 00:16:52,594
[pensive music playing]

300
00:16:52,678 --> 00:16:57,182
And about the bag stud,
they found one at their home.

301
00:17:00,102 --> 00:17:01,228
Bro…

302
00:17:02,563 --> 00:17:04,314
Bro, I'm sorry.

303
00:17:05,232 --> 00:17:06,859
I made a mistake.

304
00:17:08,861 --> 00:17:10,612
I miscalculated, bro.

305
00:17:15,075 --> 00:17:17,077
Looks like we really have to accept

306
00:17:17,161 --> 00:17:19,371
that what happened
to your sister was an accident.

307
00:17:21,457 --> 00:17:23,792
[tapping on table]

308
00:17:33,886 --> 00:17:35,262
Emerson…

309
00:17:37,097 --> 00:17:38,515
Atoy has a point.

310
00:17:40,934 --> 00:17:44,938
You know, we don't really know
why that happened to your sister.

311
00:17:45,022 --> 00:17:46,190
[melancholic music playing]

312
00:17:46,273 --> 00:17:47,900
But I'm sure

313
00:17:48,901 --> 00:17:52,738
she wouldn't want you to be angry
at someone who's actually innocent.

314
00:18:01,622 --> 00:18:02,873
[sighs]

315
00:18:02,956 --> 00:18:03,916
[clicks tongue]

316
00:18:07,169 --> 00:18:08,295
It's my fault too.

317
00:18:10,297 --> 00:18:12,132
But I can't accept that it's my fault--

318
00:18:12,216 --> 00:18:13,717
[sighs]

319
00:18:15,219 --> 00:18:16,470
Eh--

320
00:18:16,553 --> 00:18:17,846
Brother--

321
00:18:18,847 --> 00:18:20,724
I was her brother, bro.

322
00:18:20,808 --> 00:18:22,142
I'm the brother.

323
00:18:24,144 --> 00:18:25,104
[sobs]

324
00:18:25,187 --> 00:18:26,647
Wasn't I supposed to be
the one protecting her?

325
00:18:26,730 --> 00:18:28,107
You both know that.

326
00:18:28,190 --> 00:18:29,650
[sobs]

327
00:18:29,733 --> 00:18:31,068
You know that!

328
00:18:32,319 --> 00:18:34,154
Well, bro--

329
00:18:34,238 --> 00:18:37,116
I was there.
I wasn't able to do anything, bro!

330
00:18:39,201 --> 00:18:40,119
- Emerson--
- [Emerson inhales]

331
00:18:40,202 --> 00:18:43,163
And now, I'm just looking
for someone to blame!

332
00:18:43,872 --> 00:18:45,541
Bro, even the lechon,

333
00:18:45,624 --> 00:18:47,543
I want to put the blame on it!

334
00:18:47,626 --> 00:18:50,045
Stop blaming yourself. Come on.

335
00:18:50,129 --> 00:18:51,171
[sighs]

336
00:18:51,255 --> 00:18:52,422
[Atoy] 'Son…

337
00:18:52,506 --> 00:18:56,176
'Son, just think about how lucky
you were to be with her.

338
00:18:56,969 --> 00:18:59,596
It's a good thing
you reconciled with your sister.

339
00:19:01,849 --> 00:19:02,933
That's true.

340
00:19:06,270 --> 00:19:07,938
Thank you.

341
00:19:08,021 --> 00:19:09,273
Thank you, really.

342
00:19:10,357 --> 00:19:12,151
It feels like you're my brothers here.

343
00:19:12,943 --> 00:19:14,319
[chuckles]

344
00:19:14,403 --> 00:19:16,738
I love you guys. It's just not obvious.

345
00:19:16,822 --> 00:19:17,781
[chuckles softly]

346
00:19:17,865 --> 00:19:18,866
Thank you.

347
00:19:18,949 --> 00:19:20,325
'Toy, thank you.

348
00:19:22,035 --> 00:19:23,996
[deep breath]

349
00:19:24,079 --> 00:19:25,789
You're my brothers now.

350
00:19:26,623 --> 00:19:27,791
We even look alike.

351
00:19:27,875 --> 00:19:29,585
I just look better by two showers, but…

352
00:19:31,336 --> 00:19:33,005
[giggles]

353
00:19:34,798 --> 00:19:37,634
- [Paldo] There you go.
- Thank you. Thank you, bro. Thank you.

354
00:19:43,182 --> 00:19:44,224
[music fades]

355
00:19:44,308 --> 00:19:47,102
If I didn't know these clothes
belonged to Tonet,

356
00:19:47,186 --> 00:19:49,730
I'd think they were yours.

357
00:19:49,813 --> 00:19:52,191
You're almost the same size as Tonet.

358
00:19:53,400 --> 00:19:55,194
That's not my style, Mom.

359
00:19:56,361 --> 00:19:59,114
And some of those she bought,

360
00:19:59,198 --> 00:20:00,949
she said I'd wear them someday.

361
00:20:03,660 --> 00:20:04,953
You know…

362
00:20:05,829 --> 00:20:08,415
With Sis Tonet, I really felt

363
00:20:08,498 --> 00:20:10,500
how nice it is to have a sister.

364
00:20:11,168 --> 00:20:13,170
- [gentle music playing]
- [Cita inhales]

365
00:20:14,296 --> 00:20:15,631
Isn't it like

366
00:20:15,714 --> 00:20:17,633
Atoy has become your brother?

367
00:20:24,598 --> 00:20:28,518
But, it's still different
having a sister, Mom.

368
00:20:28,602 --> 00:20:30,395
Everything you want to say,

369
00:20:30,479 --> 00:20:32,522
you can really tell her.

370
00:20:34,191 --> 00:20:36,068
Brother Atoy is there too.

371
00:20:36,151 --> 00:20:39,238
But it feels like
his world is different now.

372
00:20:39,988 --> 00:20:43,909
He already has a child
and an adopted daughter.

373
00:20:47,246 --> 00:20:50,249
Oh, Noel? I thought
you were coming home tomorrow?

374
00:20:54,086 --> 00:20:56,213
We got laid off from work!

375
00:20:56,922 --> 00:20:58,840
But it's fine.

376
00:20:58,924 --> 00:21:01,218
I'm tired of being a helper.

377
00:21:02,261 --> 00:21:04,888
So, what's your plan now?

378
00:21:04,972 --> 00:21:06,431
[pensive music playing]

379
00:21:06,515 --> 00:21:07,975
Nothing.

380
00:21:08,058 --> 00:21:10,102
Rest, relax.

381
00:21:10,185 --> 00:21:13,146
Well, the money you earn
from Atoy is enough, right?

382
00:21:13,230 --> 00:21:16,108
And we still have a boarder upstairs.

383
00:21:16,191 --> 00:21:19,027
Well, just raise her rent.

384
00:21:24,283 --> 00:21:25,492
She's gone.

385
00:21:25,575 --> 00:21:26,952
Damn her then!

386
00:21:27,035 --> 00:21:28,245
She left?!

387
00:21:28,328 --> 00:21:30,747
She hasn't even paid last month's rent!

388
00:21:32,416 --> 00:21:33,458
She's dead.

389
00:21:34,376 --> 00:21:36,628
Unbelievable.

390
00:21:36,712 --> 00:21:39,673
How unlucky can you get, huh?

391
00:21:42,926 --> 00:21:45,971
Karla, buy me some beer.

392
00:21:46,054 --> 00:21:47,639
Three beers, okay!

393
00:21:47,723 --> 00:21:50,434
Cita, give her money to buy.

394
00:21:50,517 --> 00:21:51,727
Huh?

395
00:21:52,436 --> 00:21:55,772
Money to buy beers!
Give her money. Are you deaf?!

396
00:21:55,856 --> 00:21:58,942
[unsettling music playing]

397
00:22:02,362 --> 00:22:04,072
[mumbling] For beer…

398
00:22:04,156 --> 00:22:06,408
This is all I have…

399
00:22:06,491 --> 00:22:07,534
How much--

400
00:22:08,493 --> 00:22:09,828
Can you hurry up?

401
00:22:09,911 --> 00:22:11,121
Are you just going to stare at each other?

402
00:22:11,204 --> 00:22:12,622
That should be enough, here.

403
00:22:12,706 --> 00:22:15,375
[tense music playing]

404
00:22:30,974 --> 00:22:33,351
[footsteps approaching]

405
00:22:34,061 --> 00:22:36,855
Martina, um…

406
00:22:38,815 --> 00:22:42,027
I told nanny…

407
00:22:43,820 --> 00:22:46,865
to return to you the stud she found.

408
00:22:48,075 --> 00:22:49,993
I just wanted to check if…

409
00:22:50,077 --> 00:22:51,536
you've received the bag stud?

410
00:22:51,620 --> 00:22:52,788
[in English] I did.

411
00:22:53,497 --> 00:22:55,916
Imagine, it was just here at home.

412
00:22:55,999 --> 00:23:00,045
So that rock stud Atoy found at the mall,

413
00:23:00,128 --> 00:23:01,338
whose could it be?

414
00:23:02,005 --> 00:23:03,757
[in English] I guess we'll never know.

415
00:23:06,468 --> 00:23:08,095
[in English] I also…

416
00:23:10,055 --> 00:23:12,265
want to apologize.

417
00:23:12,349 --> 00:23:14,476
[pensive music playing]

418
00:23:14,559 --> 00:23:15,936
[in English] For what?

419
00:23:16,019 --> 00:23:18,605
[in English] For accusing me
of killing Tonet,

420
00:23:18,688 --> 00:23:22,317
or for being so hateful
towards me and your brother?

421
00:23:23,360 --> 00:23:24,986
[in English] You know, Audrey…

422
00:23:25,779 --> 00:23:27,322
we don't need to get along.

423
00:23:28,698 --> 00:23:31,493
But do know that I always have your back,

424
00:23:31,576 --> 00:23:32,577
because…

425
00:23:33,411 --> 00:23:35,038
we're family, right?

426
00:23:36,581 --> 00:23:38,416
[in English] Don't get me wrong, Martina.

427
00:23:38,500 --> 00:23:40,168
But just because we're family

428
00:23:40,252 --> 00:23:43,046
doesn't mean I'll side with what's wrong.

429
00:23:44,923 --> 00:23:47,509
[in English] Noted
with many thanks, Audrey.

430
00:23:48,969 --> 00:23:50,595
[Janine gasping] Mommy, Mommy!

431
00:23:50,679 --> 00:23:51,888
Oh my… My dear?

432
00:23:51,972 --> 00:23:53,807
Oh, why are you crying?

433
00:23:53,890 --> 00:23:57,102
I dreamed of Tonet. She was angry at me.

434
00:23:57,185 --> 00:23:59,187
[in English] It was just a dream, my dear.

435
00:23:59,271 --> 00:24:02,440
It's not true that Tonet
is angry at you, okay?

436
00:24:02,524 --> 00:24:04,693
Um, do you want to sleep in the room?

437
00:24:04,776 --> 00:24:06,319
We'll sleep together.

438
00:24:06,403 --> 00:24:07,904
[suspicious music playing]

439
00:24:07,988 --> 00:24:09,573
[in English] You know, Audrey, I think

440
00:24:09,656 --> 00:24:12,868
Baby Janine needs a little bit
of a breather from all this…

441
00:24:12,951 --> 00:24:14,202
trauma?

442
00:24:14,286 --> 00:24:16,746
[in English] Maybe some fresh air
would do her some good.

443
00:24:16,830 --> 00:24:18,206
Just the two of you, some…

444
00:24:19,166 --> 00:24:20,542
mommy-daughter bonding.

445
00:24:20,625 --> 00:24:21,793
[in English] What do you think?

446
00:24:21,877 --> 00:24:23,795
[sniffles]

447
00:24:24,546 --> 00:24:27,215
Mommy, let's just go on vacation.

448
00:24:27,299 --> 00:24:29,259
And my birthday is coming soon.

449
00:24:29,342 --> 00:24:31,344
Let's celebrate there instead?

450
00:24:31,428 --> 00:24:33,054
[in English] Okay, dear. Yes.

451
00:24:33,138 --> 00:24:35,015
[in English] Um, wherever you wanna go.

452
00:24:36,141 --> 00:24:38,518
Come on, let's go to the room, baby, okay?

453
00:24:38,602 --> 00:24:39,686
Don't cry anymore.

454
00:24:39,769 --> 00:24:43,857
[tense music playing]

455
00:24:47,402 --> 00:24:48,695
[electronic blipping]

456
00:24:58,246 --> 00:24:59,581
- Ouch.
- What the hell?!

457
00:24:59,664 --> 00:25:00,665
Why are you angry?

458
00:25:00,749 --> 00:25:02,292
You're the one who bumped into me.

459
00:25:02,876 --> 00:25:04,753
Hey, I do fight with kids, okay.

460
00:25:04,836 --> 00:25:06,171
[Leon] Don't test me!

461
00:25:06,254 --> 00:25:07,172
[Ibyang] <i>Oh, so--</i>

462
00:25:07,255 --> 00:25:10,008
- Tatoy, I'll row, okay!
- [Atoy, indistinct]

463
00:25:10,091 --> 00:25:12,636
Did you forget
your birthday gift to me, Ibyang?

464
00:25:12,719 --> 00:25:13,678
What's that?

465
00:25:13,762 --> 00:25:16,848
Um, she said she won't join
the boating activity anymore.

466
00:25:16,932 --> 00:25:18,391
UP NEXT

467
00:25:18,475 --> 00:25:19,309
[Audrey squeals]

468
00:25:19,392 --> 00:25:20,268
[Audrey] My scarf!

469
00:25:20,352 --> 00:25:21,436
- Mommy--
- [Audrey squeals]

470
00:25:21,519 --> 00:25:22,604
[Janine] Mommy!

471
00:25:22,687 --> 00:25:24,022
[water splashes]

472
00:25:24,105 --> 00:25:25,065
Audrey?

473
00:25:28,526 --> 00:25:29,945
Mommy!

474
00:25:30,028 --> 00:25:31,196
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

475
00:25:31,279 --> 00:25:32,739
- Audrey!
- <i>♪ Holding the scissors</i> ♪

476
00:25:32,822 --> 00:25:35,992
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

477
00:25:36,576 --> 00:25:38,578
Subtitle translation by: Rachel C. Arias
